 "script": "BioWare, the Mass Effect studio, is closing after thirty-one years. Electronic Arts told staff on Wednesday, Reuters reports. EA is cutting about four hundred jobs, roughly three percent of staff. About fifty are at BioWare in Edmonton, Canada. The next Mass Effect, still in early development, is cancelled. Here's what changed. EA went private in August in a fifty-five billion dollar buyout. Now it says it'll focus on fewer, bigger action-adventure games. So Iron Man and the next Star Wars Jedi game continue. Which BioWare game meant the most to you? Tell us below.",
